<SolutionPage
  title="Environmental Health"
  parent="Mitigate"
  oneliner="You can eat clean, train hard, and sleep well — and still be undermined by what's in your air, water, and products."
  slug="environment"
>
  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    Environmental toxic burden is one of the most underestimated drivers of chronic
    disease in men. Endocrine-disrupting compounds (phthalates, BPA, PFAS), heavy metals,
    mycotoxins from mold, and indoor air pollutants accumulate over decades and interfere
    with hormone signaling, detoxification capacity, and neurological function.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Mitigate pillar addresses environmental health through practical exposure reduction —
    not fear-based paralysis. The goal is identifying the two or three highest-load exposures
    in your specific environment and eliminating them systematically.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Home Audit</h3>
      <p>Water source, air quality, mold risk, cleaning and personal care products — a structured assessment of the most common exposure sources.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Water Filtration</h3>
      <p>A quality whole-house or point-of-use filter removes chloramines, fluoride, heavy metals, and PFAS — the highest-ROI environmental intervention.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Endocrine Disruptor Reduction</h3>
      <p>Plastics, synthetic fragrances, and conventional personal care products are the primary daily disruptor exposures for most men.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Detoxification Support</h3>
      <p>Sauna, adequate sleep, cruciferous vegetables, and gut health all support Phase I/II liver detoxification — no expensive protocols needed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</SolutionPage>
